Q1. Jenkins Pipeline for a Web Project						[25 Marks]	
Scenario:
Automate the build and deployment of a web project using Jenkins.
Task:
1. Clone GitHub repository.
2. Configure Tomcat web server.
3. Deploy the application on the WebServer
4. Create the Pipeline View using Jenkins
Expected Output:
- Jenkins files as necessary.
- Jenkins pipeline view.
- Proof of web app running locally.


✅ 1. Prerequisites (System Setup for Exam)
✔ Install/Configure Tomcat (Local System)

Download Tomcat 9 or 10

Extract into:

C:\apache-tomcat-9.0.85\


Set environment variable:

CATALINA_HOME=C:\apache-tomcat-9.0.85


Start Tomcat:

Windows: bin\startup.bat

Linux: bin/startup.sh

Access Tomcat Manager:

http://localhost:8080/manager/html


Add manager credentials in tomcat-users.xml:

<role rolename="manager-gui"/>
<role rolename="manager-script"/>
<user username="admin" password="admin" roles="manager-gui,manager-script"/>


Restart Tomcat.

🧪 2. Clone GitHub Web Project

Your project must be a MAVEN WEBAPP (generates .war file):

git clone https://github.com/<yourname>/<your-web-repo>.git


Inside Jenkins → Pipeline script from SCM:

Repository:

https://github.com/<yourname>/<your-web-repo>.git

📌 3. Jenkinsfiles (Add to repo)

Your exam requires correct Jenkinsfile syntax.
Below are the best and simplest production-style files.

✔ A. Full Declarative Pipeline (Build + Deploy to Tomcat)

Create file named Jenkinsfile in GitHub repo:

pipeline {
    agent any

    tools {
        maven 'Maven3'
        jdk 'Java17'
    }

    environment {
        TOMCAT_USER = credentials('tomcat-cred')     // Jenkins credentials ID
        TOMCAT_URL  = "http://localhost:8080/manager/text"
        APP_NAME    = "mywebapp"
    }

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                echo "Cloning GitHub repo..."
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Build WAR') {
            steps {
                echo "Building Maven Web Project"
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy to Tomcat') {
            steps {
                echo "Deploying WAR to Tomcat..."

                sh """
                curl -u ${TOMCAT_USER} \
                --upload-file target/*.war \
                "${TOMCAT_URL}/deploy?path=/${APP_NAME}&update=true"
                """
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        success {
            echo "Deployment Successful: http://localhost:8080/${APP_NAME}"
        }
        failure {
            echo "Pipeline Failed"
        }
    }
}

✔ B. Scripted Pipeline Version (Optional but good to show)

Create Jenkinsfile-scripted:

node {
    stage('Checkout') {
        checkout scm
    }

    stage('Build WAR') {
        def mvnHome = tool 'Maven3'
        sh "${mvnHome}/bin/mvn clean package"
    }

    stage('Deploy WAR to Tomcat') {
        withCredentials([usernamePassword(credentialsId: 'tomcat-cred',
                                          usernameVariable: 'USER',
                                          passwordVariable: 'PASS')]) {
            sh """
            curl -u $USER:$PASS \
            --upload-file target/*.war \
            "http://localhost:8080/manager/text/deploy?path=/mywebapp&update=true"
            """
        }
    }

    stage('Complete') {
        echo "Deployment Done"
    }
}

